IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `htta-donation`
IMPORT `htta-qa`

-- Human Tissue and Transplant Act 1982 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (htta-qa.l4): every exported question, for every
-- role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the two roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error. Each
-- question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with FALSE (the situation does not hold) and every
-- later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. Every situation input is a BOOLEAN, so the trap of
-- graffiti finding 31 cannot hide a read of it.
--
-- Every question calls a baseline export, so each case is asserted twice: once against a value worked by hand from the
-- text (most taken from the baseline's own cases, htta-cases-donation.l4, and the lives c026, d021, k097 and d092), and
-- once against the baseline export's own answer on the same facts, carried into the layer's answer type. Being on the
-- Register is entered as the deceased's expressed wish or consent under s 22(2)(a): an inference, as in the baseline.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked deceased` IS A Deceased
ASSUME `an unasked relative` IS A Relative
ASSUME `an unasked list of declarers` IS A LIST OF Practitioner
ASSUME `an unasked remover` IS A Remover
ASSUME `an unasked kind of tissue` IS A `Tissue after death`
ASSUME `an unasked consent` IS A `My consent`
ASSUME `an unasked living tissue` IS A `Living tissue`
ASSUME `an unasked purpose` IS A Purpose
ASSUME `an unasked child donation` IS A `My child's donation`
ASSUME `an unasked deal` IS A Deal
ASSUME `an unasked reason` IS A `Reason for disclosure`

`as the donor` MEANS `I may give tissue or blood, or want to know what happens to my body after I die`
`as the next of kin` MEANS `I am next of kin of a person who has died, or may soon die`
`as the parent` MEANS `I am the parent or guardian of a child under 18 who may give tissue or blood`

