§§ `For the donor, living or after death (the baseline's first seat)`

-- Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die?
-- c026: on the Register.
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die` `as the donor` `c026: Chloe at 18, on the Register, dies in hospital` EQUALS `the person's own wish or consent, which no one's objection overrides (s 22(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die` `as the donor` `c026: Chloe at 18, on the Register, dies in hospital` EQUALS (`whose consent, carried` (`Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `c026: Chloe at 18, on the Register, dies in hospital`))
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die` `as the donor` `Chloe at 18, not on the Register, no one consents` EQUALS `no one's: there is no authority to remove the tissue`
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die` `as the donor` `Chloe at 18, not on the Register, no one consents` EQUALS (`whose consent, carried` (`Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `Chloe at 18, not on the Register, no one consents`))
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die` `as the donor` `Chloe at 18, not on the Register, both parents consent` EQUALS `the consent of the senior available next of kin (s 22(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die` `as the donor` `Chloe at 18, not on the Register, both parents consent` EQUALS (`whose consent, carried` (`Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `Chloe at 18, not on the Register, both parents consent`))
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die` `as the donor` `Jake at 72, on the Register, a reportable death, no coroner's consent` EQUALS `no one's yet: the coroner must first consent (s 23)`
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die` `as the donor` `Jake at 72, on the Register, a reportable death, no coroner's consent` EQUALS (`whose consent, carried` (`Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `Jake at 72, on the Register, a reportable death, no coroner's consent`))
-- s 22(1): in hospital only.
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die` `as the donor` `Daniel at 82, on the Register, dies at home, not brought into hospital` EQUALS `no one's: there is no authority to remove the tissue`
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die` `as the donor` `Daniel at 82, on the Register, dies at home, not brought into hospital` EQUALS (`whose consent, carried` (`Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after death` `Daniel at 82, on the Register, dies at home, not brought into hospital`))
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die` `as the next of kin` `an unasked deceased` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Whose consent governs donation of my tissue after I die` `as the parent` `an unasked deceased` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Can my next of kin's objection stop my tissue being taken after I die?
-- s 22(2)(a): his own consent governs.
