§§ `For the parent or guardian of a child donor (the baseline's child-donation question; ss 11-14, 17, 19)`

-- May tissue or blood be taken from my child for another person?
#ASSERT `May tissue or blood be taken from my child for another person` `as the parent` `Jake at 14 gives bone marrow to Chloe, all conditions met` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May tissue or blood be taken from my child for another person` `as the parent` `Jake at 14 gives bone marrow to Chloe, all conditions met` EQUALS (`yes if` (`May tissue be taken from my child` `Jake at 14 gives bone marrow to Chloe, all conditions met`))
-- s 13(1): a parent must consent; s 11 says who is a parent.
#ASSERT `May tissue or blood be taken from my child for another person` `as the parent` `Jake at 14 gives bone marrow to Chloe, with his guardian's consent only` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May tissue or blood be taken from my child for another person` `as the parent` `Jake at 14 gives bone marrow to Chloe, with his guardian's consent only` EQUALS (`yes if` (`May tissue be taken from my child` `Jake at 14 gives bone marrow to Chloe, with his guardian's consent only`))
#ASSERT `May tissue or blood be taken from my child for another person` `as the parent` `Jake at 14 gives bone marrow to a school friend` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May tissue or blood be taken from my child for another person` `as the parent` `Jake at 14 gives bone marrow to a school friend` EQUALS (`yes if` (`May tissue be taken from my child` `Jake at 14 gives bone marrow to a school friend`))
-- s 12(2): never non-regenerative tissue.
#ASSERT `May tissue or blood be taken from my child for another person` `as the parent` `Jake at 14 gives a kidney to Chloe, all conditions met` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May tissue or blood be taken from my child for another person` `as the parent` `Jake at 14 gives a kidney to Chloe, all conditions met` EQUALS (`yes if` (`May tissue be taken from my child` `Jake at 14 gives a kidney to Chloe, all conditions met`))
#ASSERT `May tissue or blood be taken from my child for another person` `as the parent` `Jake at 14 gives blood, a parent consents, advised harmless, he agrees` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May tissue or blood be taken from my child for another person` `as the parent` `Jake at 14 gives blood, a parent consents, advised harmless, he agrees` EQUALS (`yes if` (`May tissue be taken from my child` `Jake at 14 gives blood, a parent consents, advised harmless, he agrees`))
